WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.720
Imagine you're on your last flask of healing searching for a checkpoint in the snowy wastes.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.880
Instead, you're met with a dramatic scene:

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.960
a circular arena with an enormous glaive planted in its center.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.400
Could it be?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.460
You turn to leave but a mist gate blocks your way.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.840
From behind you hear the chilling words:

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.220
[deeply] "You made a glaive mistake coming here."

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.880
And when you turn back, the enormous weapon is now in the hands of Glaive Master Hodir.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.920
The boss bar appears, the music begins, and your life is about to end...

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.620
...Is what I might say, if I had any new Elden Ring information to share with you.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.960
Instead, I'm just making this up.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.680
I doubt you could even imagine that we'd be here four months ago, but there's barely been any news at all.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.540
Oh, Elden Ring... You'd think someone would say something about it.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.320
But instead our hopes have just been shattered with every new convention.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.480
Gamescom: no trailers. Tokyo Game Show - nothing.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.200
Brazil Game Show... *laughter*.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.040
But look up the Reddit, and... you'd think it would be dead, right?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:14.000
But it burns. It's on fire with posts about Elden Ring, full of users so desperate for news

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.220
that they've actually started to pretend that the game is already out.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.800
There's a huge post ranking fictional bosses from easiest to hardest.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.140
Folks are discussing their favorite boss music, and

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:32.140
don't even get them started on Glaive Master Hodir's sweep into heavy attack combo.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:37.820
Glaive Master Hodir was the first boss they created, I think, and it seems like no one knows how to beat him.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:44.520
But, I do. Just like you kill any meme, the way to beat this meme boss is to make him popular.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:51.140
So, by bringing him to my audience, I hereby claim that I'm the first to defeat Glaive Master Hodir.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:54.960
All of this fake lore and fake bosses got me thinking -

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.940
since it's unlikely we'll get Elden Ring news until the Game Awards in December

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:05.340
and since everyone's going hollow waiting, let's do something to pass the time.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.580
Earlier this year, we ran the prosthetic art challenge for Sekiro - which was really fun -

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.180
and today, I'm excited to announce the first art challenge for Elden Ring.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:22.640
It's going to be an effort to give form to fictional bosses, but, they have to be inspired by regional folklore

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.860
and the limited information on Elden Ring that we already have.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:32.240
If you're interested in competing, tune in to the end of the video where I'm going to go over the finer details

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.280
and if you're not interested, keep listening, because

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.460
there is still a ton of Elden Ring news I haven't shared on this channel yet, coming soon.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.289
The prize pool for this challenge is higher this time:

00:02:43.289 --> 00:02:49.320
It's going to be two thousand US dollars and it's going to be split across the top ten participants

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.640
as shown on screen.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.260
The reason I can fund this out of my own pocket is because you guys have been

00:02:54.260 --> 00:03:00.940
insanely supportive of the sponsorship and merchandise stuff that I've been doing. Like, insanely supportive.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:08.320
So thank you. Speaking of which, this is your last chance to buy Fate, my limited edition Elden Ring inspired merch.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:14.639
I've added 48 more hours to the listing, and then this red-haired variant is gone forever.

00:03:14.739 --> 00:03:18.060
So, check it out in the description below.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.400
All the way back in June I penned a video about Elden Ring that was based on the trailer,

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.580
but a few days later, more information dropped, in interviews and in leaks.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:34.640
Despite what I said earlier, there's a lot here you might have missed and there's even more to speculate on.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:42.000
First, we have confirmation via IGN that our character will be able to traverse the world on a horse.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:47.604
If mounts are required, then it really does confirm that the scale of the world is going to be huge,

00:03:47.604 --> 00:03:50.020
because we need the mount to traverse it.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.980
This sort of scale isn't seen in any other From Software games.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.440
This could explain why the game seems to be eating up more development time than usual.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.060
Incidentally, these were some of the first leaks that we received and these leaks also suggested

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.980
that we'd be traveling to distant kingdoms in order to acquire their special powers.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:17.260
Hopefully the existence of different kingdoms implies that the game will be a truly open world from the very start.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:22.400
I feel like so many open-world games make the mistake of designing these enormous worlds

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.640
only to put the character on rails.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:32.040
Often we're restricted by the story or we're restricted by the increased difficulty in late-game areas,

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.740
but since From aren't usually restricted by story or scaling difficulty

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:42.300
I can imagine their open world being closer to something like Breath of the Wild's design,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:49.020
with areas that you can tackle in any order and with every area having its own self-contained story.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:56.380
Another common feature of open-world games are really big populated towns, but Miyazaki admits that

00:04:56.380 --> 00:05:02.380
"Creating a more open game is a big challenge for us. If we were to add towns on top of that,

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.340
it would become a bit too much,

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.280
so we decided to create an open-world-style game focused on what we're best at."

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.820
And what they're best at is definitely not populated, heavily voice-acted towns.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.880
So, "Villages will be the dark dungeon-like ruins that you've come to expect from us."

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.620
Usually, when games build really populated towns into them,

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:29.220
they often serve as a sort of reprieve from travel and combat.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:36.420
They're a chance for your character to chat and trade with NPCs and also to develop the story a little bit more.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:42.760
The closest parallel to something like this in From games are their hub worlds, like Firelink Shrine,

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:46.560
which give you a break from the endless death in the overworld.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:52.040
but if Elden Ring's open world has you doing things like gathering resources or

00:05:52.540 --> 00:06:00.220
finding traders, navigating or just looking for non-combat secrets, then, man, that's plenty of relaxation for me.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:05.440
I always get kind of bored chatting to NPC's in towns so I'm not sad to see this go.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:10.680
But I do wonder - what's their excuse going to be for everyone in the world being dead?

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:14.140
Again, maybe a sort of Ragnarok, perhaps?

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:21.160
So, while Miyazaki considers the gameplay to be in the same genre as Dark Souls, he also goes on to state that

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:26.200
"With a larger world, new systems and action mechanics inevitably become necessary.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.760
In that sense, I think that Elden Ring is a more natural evolution of Dark Souls."

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.020
"The more extensive world will form the base of Elden Ring's gameplay

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.500
and its mechanics are designed with that type of environment in mind."

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:42.920
That's pretty vague. But let me try to contextualize his statements

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.940
by using other open-world games as examples.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:50.840
So when he says that "new systems will become necessary as a result of the open world,"

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:55.940
maybe he's talking about things like preparation mechanics that make use of resources in the world,

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:58.380
like alchemy in The Witcher 3,

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:02.960
which lets you prepare for certain types of combat by giving you certain types of buffs.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.620
He could be talking about a crafting system where you create tools and weapons from the resources around you,

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:11.120
like in Horizon Zero Dawn

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:14.460
or even weapon maintenance systems like in Metro Exodus.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:20.540
He could even be talking about survival mechanics where the world itself is your enemy and is the gameplay

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:25.780
and you might need to take the weather or your hunger or body warmth into account.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.680
I suppose these are examples of the world itself forming the

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:33.580
quote-unquote "base of Elden Ring's gameplay" as Miyazaki says.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.960
Miyazaki goes on to say that larger environments will add more variation to battles.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.400
So this reminds me the most of Breath of the Wild again,

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.560
where you can use the environment in creative ways to take out groups of enemies.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.240
You can roll rocks down into their encampments,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.800
you can steal their weapons while they sleep so that they have nothing to fight you with,

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.985
you can even do crazy things like giving them metal weapons in a storm

00:07:57.985 --> 00:08:01.680
so that they get struck by lightning when they pick them up.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:07.380
Another example might be in Horizon Zero Dawn where you can set traps ahead of difficult encounters.

00:08:07.399 --> 00:08:13.800
I love this kind of stuff, and having more control of the world around you in Elden Ring, it could be huge.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.720
Another fundamental difference here is that we're going to be mounted a lot of the time,

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:24.880
so combat must be changing to suit the increased movement speed of us and our enemies.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:28.820
So, when we look at other games with mounted combat in an open world,

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.340
it usually consists of maneuvering your mount for a while,

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:40.360
and then there's a brief clash with a well-timed strike and then you maneuver again and clash and go on and on.

00:08:40.729 --> 00:08:48.609
In reality a lot of this time is usually spent sprinting past your enemy, missing and getting stuck on a tree or some terrain.

00:08:48.709 --> 00:08:55.209
For me, the best mounted combat moments usually come when some sort of slow motion or archery is involved.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.839
But I generally end up hating the whole mounted combat experience.

00:08:59.269 --> 00:09:04.628
But. If anyone can remove the awkwardness of mounted combat, it's From Software.

00:09:04.628 --> 00:09:08.300
So, I fully expect them to innovate in this space

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:14.580
Moving away from combat, Elden Ring is said to go beyond simply bringing new twists to the formula,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.000
like Bloodborne and Sekiro did.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:22.620
Now, with a larger scale, says Miyazaki, there will be more freedom and depth to exploration.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:28.340
Which I hope means there's going to be more secrets and even side quests, maybe, that aren't combat based.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:32.880
Look back at Sekiro and think about all the new verticality they added to that game.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.300
You can jump, you can grapple, swimming was incredible and...

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.880
actually, I have the feeling that these mechanics might have been a sort of beta test

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:45.200
for what will, surely, be in Elden Ring as well.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:50.300
As for navigation in Elden Ring, my only hope is that exploration

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:54.000
actually requires you to engage with the world around you.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.480
One of the worst trends in open-world games, I think, are waypoints,

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:03.880
and, there's always this focus on that little arrow that tells you where to go next.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:07.360
And as a result you sort of stop taking in the world around you?

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.920
We've never seen what a map function looks like in a From game and

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:17.420
I'm keen to see their take on it, because you can design cooler ways of interacting with the world around you

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.080
to sort of figure out where you are and where you're going.

00:10:20.389 --> 00:10:26.558
Finally, Miyazaki hopes that the world and lore can now be displayed on a grander scale.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:32.640
And with genuine distance between locations now, the world should certainly feel more real.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:37.720
And as for the lore, well, we'll have to talk about George RR Martin for that one.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.900
Of the lore we currently know very little,

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:45.900
except that the Elden Ring once served as the rules and the rhythm of the world.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:51.400
As a parallel to this, to help you understand, just think about how the Age of Fire worked in Dark Souls:

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:54.820
it was always rising and falling, but it was never-ending.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:11:00.260
And whatever the Eldon ring is, it sounds like a similar "logic of the world,"

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:06.960
but now it's been shattered, and it seems like characters are now forced to survive in a post Elden Ring world,

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:11.460
a world that Miyazaki says will showcase the will of humanity.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:17.760
So everything that occurred before this shattering - a.k.a. the lore - was actually written by George Martin.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:23.540
He wrote about a time the player wasn't directly involved in, and then passed that story on

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:30.280
to the From Software team who go on to describe his writing as a sort of guide book for the world's law.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:37.740
They say it's similar to having a Dungeon Master's Handbook in a tabletop RPG. Miyazaki says

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:41.700
"It was a fantastic collaboration, as we weren't restricted by each other,

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.760
yet we were still influenced by each other's work."

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:49.180
By having him write about a time that the player isn't directly involved in

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:53.060
he is free to unleash his creativity in the way that he likes."

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:59.340
"Furthermore, as FromSoftware we didn't want to create a more linear and story-driven experience for Elden Ring.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:05.120
So both issues could be solved by having Martin write about the world's history instead."

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:10.739
"The player will be able to learn about Martin's mythology through exploration," confirmed Miyazaki,

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:16.220
"We're known for letting the player explore the games lore through fragments of environmental storytelling,

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:21.100
and this time around Martin's story is what you'll be trying to unravel."

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.480
"The period that the player actually explores is still connected to the old times,

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:30.120
so as you slowly discover why the world has become the way it is,

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:33.600
you'll learn more about Martin's mythology as well.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.720
So, getting towards the end now,

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:42.880
any extra information we have at this point in the video is only really attainable from leaks.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:49.040
And, when it comes to leaks in the past few months, there's only really one that's worth its salt.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.160
Back in May there was this large post that was made on the ResetEra forums

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.500
by a renowned user called Omnipotent,

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:01.220
who has accurately leaked details about From Software games in the past.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:04.600
If you want to read his full post, it's in the description.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:11.020
But here are the safest takeaways from what they had to say. Take this with a grain of salt, of course.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.560
According to the leaks, the game is likely to be high fantasy,

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:20.040
which means it's quite fantastical and not grounded in reality.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:26.880
It also seems like there's going to be a very high likelihood that the game will have PvP, creative builds,

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:32.320
RPG elements and a sort of variable experience depending on how you build your character.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:38.340
These are things that Omni says will foster good, and I quote, "YouTube content."

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:42.000
He even goes and spells out Scotland at one point,

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.080
which is a region with folklore that is rarely explored in game,

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.040
and this is basically going to be the basis of the art competition -

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:54.060
seeing how we could bring folklore from this region to life.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:59.400
He also seems to make a few nods towards the same sort of vibe that Déraciné gives off,

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:04.180
with a world that is just out of view and yet present all the same.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:08.740
Think fairies and other whimsical yet sinister beings.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:13.560
It could even be inspired by William Sharp's poetry like Déraciné was.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:17.940
He says that there is so much to dig into and search for,

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:24.780
perfect for people who like to explore and discover these worlds, lore hounds and solitary soldiers.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:29.780
There's plenty of unearthed knowledge to write your paragraphs of theories about.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:34.480
Uh, that's... good, and he actually puts capital letters on "Unearthed Knowledge,"

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:39.280
so, maybe he's suggesting that there is a sort of old world to uncover?

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:42.380
Or maybe underground labyrinths to explore?

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:48.699
Towards the end, he even mentions some themes that are common with Vikings, like runes and cello horns,

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:54.760
and there was even some overlap between Viking and Celtic cultures at some point in history,

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:59.400
so it does all seem to be coming together in that region.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.680
Of course, like all leaks, we're going to have to wait and see

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:09.360
if this is validated in December before we take it all too seriously. But... I like where this is heading.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:15.120
And finally, he says this journey doesn't end with E3, this is only the beginning

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:18.400
so don't expect to be fully satiated just yet.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:23.480
But I hope this hype train will carry us there and back again, rain or shine.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.700
"Rain or shine?" Maybe he's referring to a weather system?

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:34.580
Erm, but I am more concerned that he says that the hype train "might carry us all the way back to E3."

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:40.300
If this is true then the game might actually have a later release date than we expected.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:44.320
Because, I was pretty sure they were going to show gameplay at Gamescom

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:48.940
and then I was pretty sure they were going to show it at Tokyo Game Show, but, now...

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:53.220
I'm pretty sure they're going to show gameplay at the Game Awards in December,

00:15:53.660 --> 00:16:00.300
Hopefully I'm not wrong again. As for a release date, the earliest possible would be March 2020,

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:06.100
as that's when From usually releases their games and it's the end of the fiscal year in Japan.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.579
However, their trailer releases have been later than expected.

00:16:10.579 --> 00:16:18.100
Usually we're a bit further along at this point and there aren't many big conventions at all really that are left

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:21.800
to promote the game at between now and March.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.500
Additionally, the game's scope is way bigger than recent titles,

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:31.420
so I honestly wouldn't be surprised if Elden Ring was the first title in a while to buck the trend

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.540
and it might actually be released later in the year.

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:39.780
We should all be prepared for that at least, but for now, let's move on to the art competition.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:46.039
It's gonna be something that can keep us sane and entertained if we do end up having to wait a really long time.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:50.960
The goal of this competition is to design and draw a boss.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:55.920
And the only requirement, really, is that your inspiration must be drawn

00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:00.420
from the folklore that Elden Ring is rumored to be inspired by.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:05.020
So, that's Scandinavian/Nordic folklore, Gaelic folklore,

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:09.360
Irish folklore, Celtic mythology, or even Scottish mythology.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:13.540
Of course, Elden Ring might not end up being inspired by these things at all,

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:19.900
but it's a start, and all of these places have incredible creatures and themes and stories,

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:26.260
and whether you choose just one of these sources or a mixture for your boss design is up to you.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:30.200
In the description I've listed some reading material to sort of start you off,

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.180
but I encourage you to go beyond this and look on your own as well

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:40.440
Once you've chosen your inspiration and you've drawn your piece, send it to me with a bit of a written description.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:43.200
Two things I'd like you to write in your email:

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.240
First, tell me what folklore that you were actually inspired by, and

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.600
Second, tell me a little bit about your boss fight.

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:54.560
Tell me, for example, what's its name? Where does the fight take place?

00:17:54.560 --> 00:18:00.140
Does the fight have dialog? Does it have phases? Lore? Does the boss have weaknesses?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.000
Does it make use of the open world in some way?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:07.080
If you decide to draw a background environment, is this where the fight takes place?

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:11.080
Just give me some information. Don't worry about answering all these questions,

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:16.820
I just want you to give me some idea of what the fight is like and how it reflects your boss design.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:22.560
If you're still looking for more inspiration, bear in mind that I have two videos on Elden Ring now.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:27.860
There's a cinematic, where two characters in it have sort of prosthetic arms.

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:30.800
There's two knights in this trailer that have red hair

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.820
They're all high fantasy styled knights.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:38.100
These are all sort of trends that you can maybe pull inspiration from as well,

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:40.920
so go watch the trailer, go watch my videos.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:48.540
Hell, go on the Elden Ring subreddit and look at some of the bosses that people have just made up and posted about.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:55.080
I'm sure these people would be ok with you bringing their ideas to life as long as you credit them in your email.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:59.060
I've linked some really good comments from the subreddit down below.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:04.029
Assuming this contest goes well, at least the top 10 winners will be featured in a video,

00:19:04.029 --> 00:19:08.260
and there will be special mention to other contestants as well.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:13.400
Prize distribution is as follows on screen and it will be delivered via PayPal.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:22.180
You have until midnight on the 23rd of November, PST, to email your art to eldenringchallenge@gmail.com

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.820
Remember to include a written description of the folklore you were inspired by,

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:31.600
tell me how the bossfight works, list your artist portfolio, social media

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.960
and also your PayPal address, in case you win.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:37.700
If you have any questions, don't email them.

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:42.360
Instead, head over to my Discord and go to the Elden Ring FAQ,

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.460
and see if your question has already been asked.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:49.140
If it hasn't, you can ask the question in the text channel below it.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:51.900
Thank you so much for your interest. I think this is gonna be fun.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:56.020
If you're not an artist, maybe share this competition with an artist that you know,

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.400
and... Good luck. See you in a month.

